<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

* ''HIGH — [[tools/commit-relay.mjs:42-47|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.mjs:42]]:'' `mkdir(iso)` runs before the real-path checks. If `goDir/broker-iso` resolves inside a lane or scratch tree, startup writes there before refusing. The `goDir` realpath handles a symlinked go directory; tests miss this pre-check write and symlink cases.
* ''MED — [[tools/launch-codex.mjs:80-81|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.mjs:80]]:'' Any parsed token event marks the tail fresh, even when its total is unchanged; [[line 178|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.mjs:178]] then resets blindness. Repeated unchanged totals can keep a seat alive indefinitely. Conversely, a legitimate tool run with no token events for ten minutes is stopped. Tests cover stale reads, but neither case.
* ''MED — [[tools/launch-codex.mjs:183-185|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.mjs:183]]:'' If `stop()` throws while handling a watch error—such as `kill`, `alive`, or writing `ceiling.md` failing—the catch handler rejects. The top-level `.then(...)` has no rejection handler ([[line 446|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.mjs:446]]), so the supervisor can exit without a confirmed stop. No test exercises stop failure.
* ''LOW — [[tools/seat-broker.mjs:350-355|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/seat-broker.mjs:350]]:'' Byte size is correctly capped, but UTF-8 encoding silently replaces unpaired surrogates, and NULs are accepted. Tests cover ASCII size and one trailing newline, not encoding, NUL, or newline boundaries.

<<~/ahu>>

